{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016zJVuKGesUBcFrUgogUjse","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"atomic oxygen binding energy Cu(111) fcc hollow DFT PBE eV relative to gas-phase O atom\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"InterPhon: Ab initio Interface Phonon Calculations within a 3D Electronic Structure Framework\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.04198\"},{\"title\":\"CO adsorption on Cu(111) and Cu(001) surfaces: improving site preference in DFT calculations\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0408394\"},{\"title\":\"Re-visiting the O/Cu(111) system -- When metastable surface oxides could become an issue!\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1411.0276\"},{\"title\":\"Multiple Adsorption of CO Molecules on Transition Metal Substitutional Impurities in Copper Surfaces\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.07858\"},{\"title\":\"arxiv.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.arxiv.org/pdf/2505.12914\"},{\"title\":\"P 46 a11 6122919\",\"url\":\"https://accms.mobility.niche.tohoku.ac.jp/ACCMS-11/POSTER/P-46_a11_6122919.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Structural and electronic properties of atomic oxygen adsorption on Cu(111) surface: A first-principles investigation\",\"url\":\"https://bvbvf1.bib-bvb.de/vufind/PrimoRecord/cdi_chongqing_primary_44769476\"},{\"title\":\"s11433 012 4868 5\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1007/s11433-012-4868-5.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"www.rsc.org\",\"url\":\"https://www.rsc.org/suppdata/c8/cp/c8cp04253e/c8cp04253e1.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"PhysRevB 73 165424\",\"url\":\"https://condensed.physics.usyd.edu.au/old_website/papers_aloy/PhysRevB_73_165424.pdf\"}]\n\nThe search turned up one PBE-based study that matches your setup closely, plus a few others that are less clean.\n\n- **Closest match (arXiv 2505.12914):** This paper defines binding energy relative to an isolated oxygen atom in the gas phase. Its table gives -5.000 eV for fcc and -4.905 eV for hcp. It reports that threefold hollow sites, both fcc and hcp, are the preferred sites. The fcc-hcp gap here is about 0.095 eV.\n- **Poster with a different magnitude (Tohoku ACCMS-11):** This work reports -6.37 eV and -6.26 eV for the fcc and hcp hollow sites, respectively. The snippet does not state the functional or the gas-phase reference, so I can't confirm it matches your definition. The roughly 1.4 eV gap from the -5.0 eV value is unexplained by the snippets.\n- **Other PBE/DFT context:** A VASP study using PBE says the PBE exchange-correlation functional is used, but the snippet does not give the fcc value. A separate study reports that the electronic energy of the fcc (2×2) structure is 0.13 eV lower than the hcp (2×2) at 0.25 ML coverage. Another paper (Soon et al., PRB 73, 165424) uses the opposite sign convention, where a positive number indicates that the adsorption is exothermic.\n\n**Takeaway:** Both the fcc and hcp hollow sites are favoured, with fcc slightly more stable in every source. The absolute values disagree (about -5.0 eV versus -6.3 eV), so check the functional, coverage, and reference state before relying on either number. The -5.00 eV value is the only one I could tie directly to a PBE calculation with a gas-phase O atom reference.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d545003-cc6e-4da5-a676-71f1c32de4a0","uuid":"eaea83bf-dfb2-40d2-989d-603c6623f6a9","timestamp":"2026-11-01T07:36:37.415Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"atomic oxygen binding energy Cu(111) fcc hollow DFT PBE eV relative to gas-phase O atom","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Uh3wJPNqqg7U5keqsYTrSF","content":[{"title":"InterPhon: Ab initio Interface Phonon Calculations within a 3D Electronic Structure Framework","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2012.04198"},{"title":"CO adsorption on Cu(111) and Cu(001) surfaces: improving site preference in DFT calculations","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cond-mat/0408394"