f it.\\nLITERATURE: a web search found a DFT study of O on Cu(111) (Reddy & Chatterjee, arXiv:2505.12914). A search-engine excerpt credits it with fcc -5.000 and hcp -4.905 eV vs a gas-phase O atom, with hollow sites preferred. I could not extract the PDF text, so I have NOT confirmed that paper's functional, coverage or settings. Taken at face value, the gap is about 0.16 eV, consistent with MLIP-vs-DFT error and setup differences, and well within the stated uncertainty. The ~0.1 eV fcc-hcp gap in that excerpt matches the worker's 0.05 eV in ordering and rough size. A conference poster in the same search (Tohoku ACCMS-11) reportedly gives -6.37/-6.26 eV, but its reference and functional are unclear. I treat it as non-comparable and did not rely on it.\\nLIMITATIONS: only MACE-MPA-0 is cached here, so I could not run a second MLIP. My reproduction confirms the arithmetic and protocol, not the model's independence from its training data.\\nVERDICT: pass. The value -4.84 eV (fcc, PBE-like, 1/9 ML) is reproducible and physically sensible, and it is not contradicted by the partly confirmed literature value. Read it as a PBE-level number. The true binding is probably weaker, closer to -4.3 eV, because of the O-reference error.\"}\nEOF\n./board post check @/tmp/chk/check.json --parent 13d6fb1f-73d8-4eea-b82d-711cc93021fb"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1105,"cache_read_input_tokens":28139,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1105,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d545003-cc6e-4da5-a676-71f1c32de4a0","uuid":"a2424d35-d125-4ead-b33d-aa66a28df1ef","timestamp":"2026-11-01T07:37:21.771Z","request_id":"req_011Cgbpop99RdoMAteSVEbUM","wire_tool_