:0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":14,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I posted my check (`0d9643bb-8ad3-4056-91d2-75f6f3e78514`) as a **method_audit** with verdict **pass**. The worker's value of −4.84 eV holds up, but it is a PBE-level number, and the true binding is probably weaker.\n\n- **Reproduction:** I wrote my own script with the same model (MACE-MPA-0, the only model on this machine) and same setup: 3×3 Cu(111) slab, 4 layers, 1/9 monolayer of O. My numbers match the worker's to within 0.001 eV:\n\n  | Quantity | Result |\n  |---|---|\n  | fcc hollow site | −4.837 eV |\n  | hcp hollow site | −4.783 eV |\n  | on-top site | −3.082 eV |\n  | Relative to ½ O₂ (fcc) | −1.694 eV |\n  | O₂ dissociation energy | 6.28 eV |\n\n- **Premise:** The question is well-posed as a computed 0 K binding energy, but no experiment measures it directly. The reference file `/data/calibration/tier1.json` has nothing for this property; it only holds bulk data such as melting points and densities.\n- **Method:** A static relaxation of a slab is the right approach. The weak point is the reference energy of an isolated O atom, since these models are not trained on isolated atoms. The model behaves like standard DFT (PBE) here, so it inherits PBE's known overbinding of O₂, about 0.5 eV per O atom. The worker's ±0.6 eV uncertainty covers this honestly. It spans the direct value (−4.84 eV) and a corrected estimate using the measured O₂ dissociation energy (about −4.30 eV).\n- **Literature:** A search excerpt credits [Reddy & Chatterjee, arXiv:2505.12914](https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.12914) with about −5.00 eV (fcc) and −4.91 eV (hcp), relative to a gas-phase O atom. That is within about 0.16 eV of the worker's value, with the same fcc-first site order. I could not extract the PDF text, so I have not confirmed that paper's functional or coverage, and I flagged the comparison as partial. A [poster](https://accms.mobility.niche.tohoku.ac.jp/ACCMS-11/POSTER/P-46_a11_6122919.pdf) reports about −6.4 eV with an unclear reference, so I did not rely on it.\n- **Limitation:** No second model was available offline, so this check confirms the calculation and protocol, not whether a different model would agree.\n\nSources:\n- [Reddy & Chatterjee, arXiv:2505.12914](https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.12914)\n- [Richter et al., arXiv:1411.0276](https://arxiv.org/abs/1411.0276)\n- [Tohoku ACCMS-11 poster P-46](https://accms.mobility.niche.tohoku.ac.jp/ACCMS-11/POSTER/P-46_a11_6122919.pdf)\n- [Soon et al., PRB 73, 165424](https://condensed.physics.usyd.edu.au/old_website/papers_aloy/PhysRevB_73_165424.pdf)","ttft_ms":1529,"type":"result","duration_ms":115497,"uuid":"89d549c0-4596-4dbe-94e8-f6a8442c49bb","ttft_stream_ms":835,"time_to_request_ms":182,"first_content_frame_ms":835,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":24,"outputTokens":5853,"cacheReadInputTokens":287980,"cacheCreationInputTokens":18479,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.267147,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1164,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":18479,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":99014,"outputTokens":4584,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":1,"costUSD":0.022193400000000002,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":2757,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
